---
import { Font } from "astro:assets";
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/mathbridge.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/")
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
const live = "https://mathbridge-ai.duckdns.org/";
const projectRepo = "https://github.com/jovian-2wang/mathbridge-ai-project-page";
const appRepo = "https://github.com/jovian-2wang/mathbridge-AI";
const award = "https://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/show-award/?AWD_ID=2627693";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="MathBridge AI helps students work through Math 6 problems, while teachers and families see useful next steps." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={`${base}favicon.svg`} />
    <Font cssVariable="--font-noto-sans" preload={[{ subset: "latin", style: "normal" }]} />
    <title>MathBridge AI | Math learning, step by step</title>
  </head>
  <body class="mb-page font-(family-name:--font-noto-sans)">
    <header class="mb-header" id="top">
      <div class="mb-nav mb-shell">
        <a class="mb-brand" href="#top">MathBridge <b>AI</b></a>
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#student">For students</a><a href="#teacher-family">For teachers & families</a><a href="#how-built">How it works</a>
        </nav>
        <a class="mb-nav-cta" href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open MathBridge ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="mb-partners">
        <div class="mb-shell mb-partner-row">
          <a href="https://www.utsa.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src={`${base}brands/ut-san-antonio-logo.svg`} alt="The University of Texas at San Antonio" /></a>
          <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <a href="https://www.ufl.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src={`${base}brands/uf-logo-full.png`} alt="University of Florida" /></a>
          <a class="mb-award" href={award} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NSF Award 2627693 ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mb-shell mb-hero">
        <div>
          <p class="mb-kicker">MATH 6 · STUDENT FIRST</p>
          <h1>Try it. Find the tricky step. Try again.</h1>
          <p class="mb-lead">MathBridge starts with the student's class problem. It helps them work out the next step without doing the math for them.</p>
          <div class="mb-buttons"><a class="mb-button mb-button-primary" href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Try the live platform ↗</a><a class="mb-button" href={projectRepo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Project website code</a><a class="mb-text-link" href={award} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NSF project ↗</a></div>
          <p class="mb-private">Platform source: <a href={appRepo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">private project repository ↗</a></p>
        </div>
        <aside class="mb-hero-card" aria-label="Example student task">
          <span class="mb-label">A MATH 6 QUESTION</span>
          <h2>24 points in 3 games. How many points per game?</h2>
          <div class="mb-student-write"><span>THE STUDENT TRIES</span><b>24 ÷ 3 = 6</b></div>
          <div class="mb-clue"><span>A CLUE, IF THEY NEED ONE</span><b>“If each game had 6 points, how many points would that be altogether?”</b></div>
          <small>Student thinks → gets a clue → tries again</small>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section id="student" class="mb-section mb-student-section">
        <div class="mb-shell">
          <div class="mb-section-heading"><p class="mb-kicker">01 · THE STUDENT'S CLASSWORK COMES FIRST</p><h2>Help with the step that is hard.</h2><p>The class question and its math goal stay in charge. Help changes to fit what the student needs next.</p></div>
          <div class="mb-learning-path" aria-label="Student learning steps">
            <div><span>1</span><section><b>Class question</b><p>Start with the Math 6 task.</p></section></div>
            <div><span>2</span><section><b>Student tries</b><p>Keep the student's own work.</p></section></div>
            <div><span>3</span><section><b>Find the hard part</b><p>Check the math idea behind the answer.</p></section></div>
            <div><span>4</span><section><b>Give the next help</b><p>A clear hint, a picture, or a reminder of an earlier skill.</p></section></div>
            <div><span>5</span><section><b>Try again</b><p>Use a similar question to check if the student can do it on their own.</p></section></div>
          </div>
          <div class="mb-two-notes">
            <article><span class="mb-label">IF A STUDENT IS STUCK</span><h3>Help builds one step at a time.</h3><p>Make the question clear → connect to something they know → show a picture → guide the next step → model part of it. Then ask them to try again without the hint.</p></article>
            <article class="mb-grade-note"><span class="mb-label">CHECK THE EARLIER SKILL, IF NEEDED</span><h3>Start with Grade 6. Look back only when the work points there.</h3><p>If a student is stuck, MathBridge checks the related Grade 5 skill. If that is also hard, it checks the Grade 4 foundation. Then it helps at that level and returns to the Grade 6 goal.</p></article>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-interest-demo" id="interest-demo">
            <div class="mb-interest-copy"><p class="mb-kicker">STUDENT CHOICES</p><h2>Pick more than one thing you like.</h2><p>Choose up to three interests. In a new practice question, MathBridge can use one you picked for the story, so the example feels familiar. In Course Mode, the reviewed class question stays the same.</p><p class="mb-keep-math"><b>The math stays the same.</b> A similar practice question keeps the skill, but uses new numbers and a different story.</p></div>
            <div class="mb-interest-box">
              <fieldset>
                <legend>Things I like <small>Choose up to 3</small></legend>
                <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="basketball" checked /> Basketball</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="baking" /> Baking</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="games" /> Video games</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="music" /> Music</label>
                <label><input type="checkbox" name="interest" value="animals" /> Animals</label>
              </fieldset>
              <div class="mb-similar-example"><span class="mb-label">A SIMILAR QUESTION COULD BE · USING ONE YOU PICKED</span><p id="similar-question">A basketball player scores 32 points in 4 games. How many points per game?</p><small id="similar-skill">Same skill: find the amount for 1 game.</small></div>
              <p class="mb-interest-limit">Your choices can change the story in practice. They do not change the class task, math skill, or right answer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mb-preference-row">
            <article><span class="mb-label">LANGUAGE</span><h3>Understand the words.</h3><p>Keep the English question. Add Chinese or Spanish to explain hard words, so the student can focus on the math.</p><div class="mb-example-translation"><b>unit rate</b><span>单位率 / tarifa unitaria</span></div></article>
            <article><span class="mb-label">READ ALOUD</span><h3>Listen when reading is hard.</h3><p>The student presses Play to hear the question or help. Nothing starts talking by surprise.</p><div class="mb-example-translation"><b>Question or hint</b><span>Tap ▶ Play to listen</span></div></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="teacher-family" class="mb-section mb-people-section">
        <div class="mb-shell">
          <div class="mb-section-heading"><p class="mb-kicker">02 · THREE VIEWS, THREE CLEAR JOBS</p><h2>What each person can do with the learning information.</h2></div>
          <div class="mb-people-grid">
            <article class="mb-person mb-person-student"><div class="mb-person-top"><span>STUDENT</span><b>Do the math with help when needed</b></div><ul><li>Work on the class task or choose free practice.</li><li>Ask for a hint or picture.</li><li>Try again and practice the same skill.</li></ul><p class="mb-person-result">The student does the thinking and gets another chance.</p></article>
            <article class="mb-person mb-person-teacher"><div class="mb-person-top"><span>TEACHER</span><b>Decide what to teach next</b></div><ul><li>Open one student's learning record or the class overview.</li><li>See recent work, skill progress, and common mistakes.</li><li>Get a teaching focus and next-step suggestions; use linked STAAR practice when available.</li></ul><p class="mb-person-result">Plan a focused lesson or small group from what students actually did.</p></article>
            <article class="mb-person mb-person-family"><div class="mb-person-top"><span>PARENT / FAMILY</span><b>Know how to help at home</b></div><ul><li>See what is going well and what the child is practicing.</li><li>Get a question to ask and what reasoning to listen for.</li><li>Use a short home practice set; answers stay in the parent section.</li></ul><p class="mb-person-result">Have a helpful 10-minute practice together, without guessing what to teach.</p></article>
          </div>
          <p class="mb-data-note">Teachers see learning patterns for teaching. Families see a short, plain-language update. Neither has to interpret a wall of raw student data.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how-built" class="mb-section mb-built-section">
        <div class="mb-shell">
          <div class="mb-section-heading"><p class="mb-kicker">03 · HOW MATHBRIDGE HELPS A STUDENT LEARN</p><h2>One learning cycle. The next step comes from the student's evidence.</h2><p>A Math 6 course task, a free math question, or a vocabulary question can enter the cycle. The system looks for what is getting in the way, teaches what is missing, and checks learning again.</p></div>
          <figure class="mb-cycle-figure" aria-labelledby="cycle-caption">
            <svg class="mb-cycle-svg" viewBox="0 0 1240 1000" role="img" aria-labelledby="cycle-title cycle-desc">
              <title id="cycle-title">MathBridge's evidence-led learning cycle and Grade 4 to Grade 6 prerequisite path</title>
              <desc id="cycle-desc">A circular cycle starts with a course task or free question, collects student work, diagnoses vocabulary, skill, misconception, or prerequisite needs, teaches one targeted next step, checks independently, and uses new evidence to decide what comes next. The center shows targeted movement from Grade 6 to a mapped Grade 5 prerequisite and, only when needed, a mapped Grade 4 foundation, then back up to Grade 6.</desc>
              <defs>
                <marker id="cycle-arrow" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="5" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#b96543" /></marker>
                <marker id="cycle-up-arrow" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="8" refY="5" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" fill="#176678" /></marker>
              </defs>
              <path class="mb-cycle-orbit" d="M620 126 C858 126 1064 282 1064 490 C1064 702 866 868 620 868 C374 868 176 702 176 490 C176 282 382 126 620 126" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M728 155 C790 163 836 187 865 216" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M1025 400 C1044 447 1044 499 1024 548" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M854 735 C813 774 769 794 725 805" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M516 805 C469 793 426 772 385 737" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M216 548 C196 499 196 448 216 399" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-cycle-arrow" d="M385 218 C427 182 470 163 517 154" marker-end="url(#cycle-arrow)" />

              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-course"><circle cx="620" cy="140" r="108" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="620" cy="63" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="620" y="69">1</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="620" y="119">START WITH A QUESTION</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="620" y="146"><tspan x="620">Math 6 course task</tspan><tspan x="620" dy="22">or free math / vocabulary</tspan><tspan x="620" dy="22">question</tspan></text></g>
              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-evidence"><circle cx="940" cy="300" r="110" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="940" cy="222" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="940" y="228">2</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="940" y="282">STUDENT TRIES</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="940" y="310"><tspan x="940">Answer · steps · explanation</tspan><tspan x="940" dy="22">and help already used</tspan></text></g>
              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-diagnose"><circle cx="940" cy="650" r="116" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="940" cy="567" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="940" y="573">3</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="940" y="627">DIAGNOSE THE BARRIER</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="940" y="656"><tspan x="940">Vocabulary? Target skill?</tspan><tspan x="940" dy="22">Possible misconception?</tspan><tspan x="940" dy="22">A mapped prerequisite?</tspan></text></g>
              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-teach"><circle cx="620" cy="840" r="112" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="620" cy="760" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="620" y="766">4</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="620" y="824">TEACH WHAT IS MISSING</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="620" y="853"><tspan x="620">A word · a math idea · a hint</tspan><tspan x="620" dy="22">An approved picture or short</tspan><tspan x="620" dy="22">prerequisite lesson</tspan></text></g>
              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-check"><circle cx="300" cy="650" r="116" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="300" cy="567" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="300" y="573">5</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="300" y="627">CHECK INDEPENDENTLY</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="300" y="656"><tspan x="300">A targeted probe or new</tspan><tspan x="300" dy="22">similar problem, with</tspan><tspan x="300" dy="22">less or no help</tspan></text></g>
              <g class="mb-cycle-node mb-node-next"><circle cx="300" cy="300" r="110" /><circle class="mb-step-dot" cx="300" cy="222" r="18" /><text class="mb-step-num" x="300" y="228">6</text><text class="mb-node-title" x="300" y="282">USE THE NEW EVIDENCE</text><text class="mb-node-copy" x="300" y="310"><tspan x="300">Ready? Move forward.</tspan><tspan x="300" dy="22">Not yet? Adjust support</tspan><tspan x="300" dy="22">and run the cycle again.</tspan></text></g>

              <circle class="mb-path-ring" cx="620" cy="493" r="176" />
              <text class="mb-path-kicker" x="620" y="365">TARGETED PREREQUISITE PATH</text>
              <text class="mb-path-sub" x="620" y="388">Only go back when evidence points to a gap</text>
              <path class="mb-level-arrow" d="M480 562 L480 540" marker-end="url(#cycle-up-arrow)" />
              <path class="mb-level-arrow" d="M480 487 L480 465" marker-end="url(#cycle-up-arrow)" />
              <circle class="mb-level-dot mb-g4" cx="480" cy="590" r="28" /><circle class="mb-level-dot mb-g5" cx="480" cy="515" r="28" /><circle class="mb-level-dot mb-g6" cx="480" cy="440" r="28" />
              <text class="mb-level-grade" x="480" y="446">G6</text><text class="mb-level-grade" x="480" y="521">G5</text><text class="mb-level-grade" x="480" y="596">G4</text>
              <text class="mb-level-copy mb-level-detail" x="525" y="434"><tspan x="525">Math 6 ratio / rate goal</tspan><tspan x="525" dy="16">Original course task</tspan></text>
              <text class="mb-level-copy mb-level-detail" x="525" y="508"><tspan x="525">Mapped Math 5 prerequisite</tspan><tspan x="525" dy="16">Pass → return to G6</tspan></text>
              <text class="mb-level-copy mb-level-detail" x="525" y="583"><tspan x="525">Mapped Math 4 foundation</tspan><tspan x="525" dy="16">Only if G5 check still shows a gap</tspan></text>
              <text class="mb-path-rule" x="620" y="635">Teach + independently check; then build back up.</text>
              <text class="mb-path-warning" x="620" y="658">One wrong answer is evidence—not a diagnosis.</text>
            </svg>
            <figcaption id="cycle-caption">The outer loop repeats as the student learns. The center shows the prerequisite route: G5 is checked first; G4 is checked only if the independent G5 check still shows a gap. Each level is checked before moving back up.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="mb-cycle-rules">
            <p><b>Vocabulary barrier</b><span>Explain the word, then return to the math question.</span></p>
            <p><b>Possible misconception</b><span>Use a targeted confirmation problem before treating the pattern as confirmed.</span></p>
            <p><b>Missing knowledge</b><span>Teach the mapped prerequisite, check it independently, and return upward when the student is ready.</span></p>
          </div>
          <details class="mb-answer-method"><summary>Where the Math 6 Answer Edition fits</summary><p>The Student Edition course task stays primary. The Answer Edition is a reference for checking that prepared support is mathematically accurate; its answer is not handed to the student as a hint.</p></details>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-demo-strip"><div class="mb-shell"><div><p class="mb-kicker">SEE IT IN THE PLATFORM</p><h2>Try the student, teacher, or parent view.</h2><p>Open the working MathBridge platform and choose your view.</p></div><a class="mb-button mb-button-primary" href={live} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open MathBridge ↗</a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="mb-footer"><div class="mb-shell"><span>MathBridge AI · Math learning support for students, teachers, and families</span><div><a href={projectRepo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Project page code</a><a href={award} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NSF Award 2627693</a></div></div></footer>

    <script is:inline>
      (() => {
        const choices = [...document.querySelectorAll('input[name="interest"]')];
        const question = document.getElementById("similar-question");
        const skill = document.getElementById("similar-skill");
        const examples = {
          basketball: ["A basketball player scores 32 points in 4 games. How many points per game?", "Same skill: find the amount for 1 game."],
          baking: ["A baker puts 30 cookies equally on 5 trays. How many cookies on each tray?", "Same skill: find the amount for 1 tray."],
          games: ["You earn 42 game coins in 6 rounds. How many coins per round?", "Same skill: find the amount for 1 round."],
          music: ["A band plays 18 songs in 3 sets. How many songs per set?", "Same skill: find the amount for 1 set."],
          animals: ["A shelter feeds 28 dogs equally in 4 groups. How many dogs in each group?", "Same skill: find the amount for 1 group."]
        };
        const update = (changed) => {
          const selected = choices.filter((item) => item.checked);
          if (selected.length > 3) { changed.checked = false; return; }
          const chosen = changed.checked ? changed.value : selected[0]?.value;
          if (chosen && examples[chosen]) {
            question.textContent = examples[chosen][0];
            skill.textContent = examples[chosen][1];
          } else {
            question.textContent = "A class has 36 notebooks for 6 tables. How many notebooks for each table?";
            skill.textContent = "Same skill: find the amount for 1 table.";
          }
        };
        choices.forEach((item) => item.addEventListener("change", () => update(item)));
      })();
    </script>

    <style>
      :global(html) { scroll-behavior:smooth; }
      :global(body) { margin:0; background:#fff; color:#183143; }
      :global(.mb-page main) { margin:0; max-width:none; }
      .mb-page { --ink:#183143; --muted:#506575; --teal:#176678; --teal-light:#e8f3f4; --line:#d4e0e4; --warm:#bd623d; --warm-pale:#fff3ec; --green:#2f715d; font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; }
      .mb-shell { width:min(1480px, calc(100% - 80px)); margin-inline:auto; }
      .mb-header { background:#fff; }
      .mb-nav { min-height:70px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:28px; border-bottom:1px solid #e5ebed; }
      .mb-brand { color:var(--ink); text-decoration:none; font-size:20px; font-weight:800; white-space:nowrap; }.mb-brand b { color:var(--warm); }
      .mb-nav nav { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:clamp(16px,3vw,42px); }.mb-nav nav a,.mb-text-link { color:#455c6c; text-decoration:none; font-size:14px; font-weight:650; }.mb-nav nav a:hover,.mb-text-link:hover { color:var(--teal); }
      .mb-nav-cta { color:white; background:var(--ink); padding:12px 18px; text-decoration:none; font-size:13px; font-weight:750; white-space:nowrap; }
      .mb-partners { border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }.mb-partner-row { min-height:72px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:24px; }.mb-partner-row>a:first-child img { width:164px; max-height:43px; object-fit:contain; }.mb-partner-row>a:nth-of-type(2) img { width:178px; max-height:46px; object-fit:contain; }.mb-partner-row>span { height:32px; border-left:1px solid #c7d4d8; }.mb-award { margin-left:auto; color:#5a6f7b; text-decoration:none; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; }
      .mb-hero { padding:60px 0 66px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:1.15fr .85fr; gap:clamp(40px,7vw,108px); align-items:center; }.mb-kicker { color:#a95535; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; font-weight:850; letter-spacing:.15em; margin:0 0 16px; }.mb-hero h1 { max-width:800px; color:var(--ink); font-size:clamp(42px,5.2vw,74px); line-height:1.04; letter-spacing:-.045em; margin:0; }.mb-lead { max-width:680px; color:#4c6270; font-size:20px; line-height:1.55; margin:22px 0 24px; }.mb-buttons { display:flex; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; }.mb-button { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:48px; padding:0 17px; border:1px solid #9aaeb7; color:var(--ink); text-decoration:none; font-size:14px; font-weight:750; }.mb-button-primary { color:#fff; border-color:var(--teal); background:var(--teal); }.mb-button-primary:hover { background:#105565; }.mb-private { color:#7b8b93; font-size:12px; margin:17px 0 0; }.mb-private a { color:#607783; }
      .mb-hero-card { padding:30px; border:1px solid #bfd1d6; box-shadow:10px 10px 0 #eaf2f3; background:#f8fbfb; }.mb-label { display:block; color:#55747e; font-size:10px; font-weight:850; letter-spacing:.13em; }.mb-hero-card h2 { font-size:24px; line-height:1.35; margin:12px 0 22px; color:var(--ink); }.mb-student-write,.mb-clue { padding:14px 16px; }.mb-student-write { background:#e8f3f4; }.mb-clue { background:#fff2eb; margin-top:10px; }.mb-student-write span,.mb-clue span { display:block; color:#697d84; font-size:10px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.1em; margin-bottom:6px; }.mb-student-write b,.mb-clue b { display:block; color:#244655; font-size:15px; line-height:1.45; }.mb-hero-card>small { display:block; color:#55747e; text-align:center; font-size:12px; font-weight:700; margin-top:17px; }
      .mb-section { padding:78px 0; }.mb-student-section { background:#f2f7f8; }.mb-section-heading { max-width:900px; margin-bottom:30px; }.mb-section-heading h2,.mb-interest-copy h2,.mb-demo-strip h2 { margin:0; color:var(--ink); font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,49px); letter-spacing:-.035em; line-height:1.1; }.mb-section-heading>p:last-child { max-width:830px; color:var(--muted); font-size:17px; line-height:1.55; margin:14px 0 0; }
